statement:
Let n >= 1 and l be natural numbers and p > n real. Let mu be a measure on R^(n+l), H : R^(n+l) -> R^(n+l), w : R^(n+l) -> R, y in R^(n+l), R > 0 and 0 < Lambda <= 1. Write r_x := |x - y|, phi' := deriv phi for a function phi, and kappa := (p - n)/(4p). Assume:
- mu(B_R(y)) < infinity (closed ball), and H is mu-integrable on B_R(y);
- (ofReal(R^(p-n)) * lower integral over B_R(y) of |H|^p dmu)^(1/p) <= ofReal(kappa Lambda);
- w is a.e.-strongly measurable for mu restricted to ball y R, and 0 <= w(x) <= 1 for mu-a.e. x in ball y R;
- radial identity: for every C^1 function phi : R -> R and every T with phi(t) = 1 for t <= 1 and phi(t) = 0 for t >= T, and every rho > 0 with T rho < R, integral (n phi(r_x/rho) + (r_x/rho) phi'(r_x/rho)(1 - w(x))) dmu = - integral phi(r_x/rho)(x - y).H(x) dmu.
For F : R -> R put Phi(r) := F(r) (r^n)^(-1) mu(B_r(y)).toReal + F(r) - 1, and let alpha' := 1 - n/p. Then there is F : R -> R such that:
(i) for every r in (0, R): exp(-Lambda) <= F(r) <= exp(Lambda) and |F(r) - 1| <= Lambda (r/R)^(alpha');
(ii) for all 0 < s <= r < R: Phi(s) <= Phi(r), and the lower integral over B_r(y) minus B_s(y) of ofReal(w(x)/|x - y|^n) dmu is at most ofReal(exp(Lambda)(Phi(r) - Phi(s))).
